# `.claude/kit.toml`, key by key

The kit's CLI, hooks and CI read `.claude/kit.toml`. Unknown keys are errors, so a typo can't
silently switch a rule off. The installer writes only what every project needs; this page has
every other table, with an example to copy. Each example is valid as written.

## `[project]`

`name`, `test_command` (run by `lanes finish` and CI) and `integration_branch` (where finished work
lands) are set by the installer. The lane settings below are optional; these are their defaults:

<!-- example: project-lanes -->
```toml
[project]
merge_mode = "pr"                    # "pr": finished tasks become pull requests; "local": fast-forward
worktree_root = ".claude/worktrees"  # where lane folders go; "../{project}-lanes" puts them beside
ownership = "ask"                    # an edit outside the lane's paths asks you first; "off": never
shared_defaults = true               # false: drop the default [[shared]] tables (see Shared paths)
```

## `[protected]`: what agents may not touch

`{{kit_command}} settings sync` writes these as rules in `.claude/settings.json`, which Claude Code
enforces; a hook catches command forms the rules miss; pre-commit and CI report changes to
protected paths. What this stops and what it doesn't: [protected-paths.md](protected-paths.md).
After editing the table, run `{{kit_command}} settings sync`.

- `paths`: agents may not edit these, e.g. `["vendor/**", "docs/originals/"]`.
- `commands`: agents may not run these; flags match in any order. The defaults block force pushes,
  hard resets and skipped hooks. The `gh` label commands are there because the
  `kit:protected-change` label lets a protected change pass CI, and only a person adds it;
  `gh alias` could hide any of them, and `gh pr merge --admin` merges past red required checks.
- `secrets`: agents may neither read nor edit these; add your key files. `"!name"` exempts a bare
  file name listed after the names it cancels.
- `guard_kit = true` (the default): edits to the kit's own config need your approval; `false` turns
  that off.

## `[[checks.rules]]`: forbidden patterns

Checked after every agent edit, before each commit and in CI. Run them by hand with
`{{kit_command}} check rules`.

<!-- example: rules -->
```toml
[[checks.rules]]
id = "no-print"
pattern = '\bprint\('             # Python regular expression, matched line by line
paths = ["src/**/*.py"]           # gitignore-style globs from the project root
exclude = ["src/cli/**"]          # optional
message = "Use the logger, not print()."
ignore_comments = true            # optional (default true): skip matches inside comments
```

## `[hooks]`: switching a hook off

Re-running the installer puts back a kit hook you deleted from `.claude/settings.json`; switch one
off here instead, then re-run it. The protected hook is the backstop behind `[protected]` and has
no switch; the ownership hook's is `ownership = "off"` in `[project]`. A mistake in this table (a
misspelt key, `protected = false`) blocks every agent command and file edit until it's fixed.

<!-- example: hooks -->
```toml
[hooks]
rules_check = true                # check the [[checks.rules]] patterns after every agent edit
lane_router = true                # tell the agent its lane at session start
```

## `[[shared]]`: paths every lane may change

No one lane owns a shared path, and every lane may add files there. The first two tables are the
defaults: you get them without writing them, and the tables you write add to them. A table can make
a default stricter; to drop or loosen one or give it a steward, set `shared_defaults = false` in
`[project]` and write the tables you want. A `shared_paths` list in `[project]` (v0.1, mode
`"open"`) replaces the defaults unless you also set `shared_defaults = true`. A path in two tables
takes the stricter mode. Guide: [parallel-lanes.md](parallel-lanes.md).

<!-- example: shared-defaults -->
```toml
[[shared]]
paths = ["docs/changelog.d/**", "docs/health/**"]
mode = "append"                   # adding a file is free; changing or deleting one asks you

[[shared]]
paths = ["docs/backlog/**", "docs/plans/**", "docs/design/decisions-log.md"]
mode = "open"                     # any lane changes them
```

<!-- example: shared-repo-wide -->
```toml
[[shared]]
paths = ["/.gitignore", "/package.json"]  # repo-wide files, for example
mode = "ask"                      # every change asks you
steward = "core"                  # optional: the one lane that changes them without asking
```

## `[[lanes]]`: one per agent working at once

Each lane is a git worktree with its own paths. `{{kit_command}} lanes suggest` prints tables
guessed from your folders; check them, add them here, commit, then run
`{{kit_command}} lanes create`. When a lane's tests don't sit beside its code, give it their folder
too: a lane that owns only `public/**` puts its tests in `public/`, where the web server serves
them. Guide: [parallel-lanes.md](parallel-lanes.md).

<!-- example: lanes -->
```toml
[[lanes]]
name = "core"                     # lowercase letters, digits and '-': a folder name and branch prefix
scope = "Domain logic and its tests"
owns = ["src/core/**", "tests/core/**"]  # where two lanes match a file, the more specific pattern owns it
resources = { dev_port = 8001 }   # free-form; the agent is told each value at session start

[[lanes]]
name = "api"
scope = "HTTP layer"
owns = ["src/api/**", "tests/api/**"]
resources = { dev_port = 8002 }
```
